# Vault protocol

This vault is a curated project-memory and navigation layer. It is not a passive document folder,
an automatic decision maker, or a replacement for source code and review.

## Information hierarchy

| Level | Purpose | Typical source |
|---|---|---|
| L1 — orientation | Current mission and handoff | `context/goals.md`, `context/CURRENT.md`, latest session log |
| L2 — map | Locate the relevant owner | [[00-INDEX]], [[Roadmap & Status]], `find` |
| L3 — source of truth | Read the actual rule, plan, or decision | vision, requirements, invariant, ADR, or spec |
| L4 — implementation evidence | Confirm exact behavior | focused source, test, configuration, migration, or external evidence |

Generated briefs and maps accelerate L1/L2 but are never the authority. Do not assume a particular
agent runtime automatically loads context or runs a hook.

## Read protocol

Before a task:

1. Read `context/goals.md`, `context/CURRENT.md`, and the latest dated context log.
2. Start from [[00-INDEX]] or a generated brief and find the smallest owning note.
3. Read the relevant section, ADR, or feature spec before opening broad implementation source.
4. Use focused source evidence only when verifying or editing behavior.

## Write and promotion protocol

Updating durable knowledge is part of done. Put the changed fact in its canonical owner:

- Product outcome, user, scope, or non-goal → [[business/vision-and-goals|Product vision and goals]].
- Product obligation or release guardrail → [[business/requirements|Product requirements]].
- Priority, status, blocker, or evidence exit → [[Roadmap & Status|Roadmap & Status]].
- Refactor-resistant boundary or property → [[architecture/invariants|Architecture invariants]].
- Durable trade-off → [[decisions/README|Decision log]].
- Feature contract and delivery plan → [[specs/README|Feature specs index]].

Also record concrete work in a dated context log. Keep `CURRENT.md` short and replace it when the
active focus changes; it must never become a second roadmap.

Start a new curated note from [[note-template]] and select the note type that owns its fact.

## Context zone

`context/` is an append-preserving inbox for orientation, handoffs, logs, drafts, and retained
history. It is excluded from curated graph and ranked retrieval truth. Promote mature knowledge to
the owning curated note and leave the context entry as history.

## Generated output and validation

The explicit build command is the normal writer for generated vault output. Check, retrieval, and
diagnostic commands must remain read-only so they are safe in CI and optional hooks.

```sh
{{QUALITY_COMMANDS}}
```

If curated notes, source-fact inputs, configuration, or the chosen adapter change, rebuild before
strict validation. Start new integrity rules as visible findings; make them blocking only after a
clean, understood baseline and documented remediation path.

## Decision supersession sweep

When a decision changes, search durable notes for the old statement and update every relevant
duplicate in the same task. A contradiction between a decision and another canonical note is a
defect, not harmless history.

## Extension boundary

Source adapters, CI, hooks, runtime integrations, and evidence collection are optional. They must
be explicitly enabled, have an owner, and never gain authority to make production changes.
